# Copy to ~/apps/little-heroes.env on the Pi (chmod 600).
PORT=3000
# Piper + whisper.cpp on the Pi (Rex's voice and the /voice-lab.html test page)
PIPER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5000
WHISPER_CPP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8178
# Parent chore/reward alerts (server/ntfyService.js). Subscribe to this topic in the ntfy app.
NTFY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090
NTFY_TOPIC=little-heroes
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Publish-only ntfy token (ntfy user littleheroes-app, write-only little-heroes); see scripts/pi/README
NTFY_TOKEN=
# Shared secret App Hosting uses to relay Rex's voice to this Pi (= PI_RELAY_TOKEN there)
LOCAL_AI_RELAY_TOKEN=
# Umami page views (website id from the Umami dashboard)
VITE_UMAMI_HOST=https://meshlink.tail9d175a.ts.net/umami
VITE_UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID=
# Sunday 6 PM parent report (scripts/pi/weekly-report.mjs + little-heroes-weekly-report.timer).
# The household sync code(s) shown in the Parent Portal, comma-separated.
HOUSEHOLD_CODES=
# REPORT_TIME_ZONE=America/New_York
# Rex function calling (server/rexAgentService.js) uses GEMINI_API_KEY; optional model override:
# REX_AGENT_MODEL=gemini-3.7-flash
# Family Google Calendar -> "get ready" chores the night before (server/calendarService.js) and
# the Fridge Display's "Coming up" list. Google Calendar > Settings > your calendar >
# "Secret address in iCal format". Keep it secret (it is a read link to the calendar).
GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ICS_URL=
# CALENDAR_TIME_ZONE=America/New_York
# Meal Planner (server/mealsService.js, docs/meal-planner-api.md). School menus come from
# MealViewer with no key. The school is set in Parent Portal > Meal Planner; this is only the
# fallback before anyone picks one:
# SCHOOL_MENU_SLUG=CanterburyStreetMagnet
# Meal Planner API for linked apps (e.g. a recipe vault): /api/meals/v1 needs this bearer token.
# Make one with: openssl rand -hex 32   (leave empty to keep the API off)
MEALS_API_TOKEN=
# Browser apps on other sites allowed to call /api/meals/v1 (comma-separated https origins):
# MEALS_API_ORIGINS=https://recipes.example.com
# Fridge "what to wear" card and weather get-ready chores (Open-Meteo, no key). Default is
# Canterbury Street Magnet in Worcester; set both to forecast somewhere else:
# WEATHER_LAT=42.2459
# WEATHER_LON=-71.8059
# District no-school days: refreshed each summer by little-heroes-school-calendar.timer into
# this file (default shown). The 2026-27 year is also built into the app.
# SCHOOL_CALENDAR_FILE=/home/meshlink/apps/little-heroes-school-calendar.json
# Fridge extras: NASA space picture of the day. DEMO_KEY works for one fetch a day; a free
# key from https://api.nasa.gov raises the limit. The "On this day" fact uses GEMINI_API_KEY
# to retell it for kids (a strict word filter is used without it).
# NASA_API_KEY=DEMO_KEY

# Math Lab: where scripts/pi/phet-sims.mjs keeps the PhET sims (served at /phet/). Default ~/apps/phet
# PHET_DIR=/home/meshlink/apps/phet

# Voice extras (scripts/pi/setup-voice-extras.sh): Kokoro reads bedtime stories ahead of time and
# Moonshine checks Read-Along reading. Both default to the local service; set to "off" to disable.
# KOKORO_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5010
# MOONSHINE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5010
# KOKORO_VOICE=af_heart
# STORY_AUDIO_DIR=/home/meshlink/apps/story-audio

# Screen checks after each deploy (scripts/pi/screens/run-screens.sh, run by deploy-pi.yml).
# Pictures of the Fridge Display and kid screens are kept here and compared with the last deploy.
# Run "bash ~/apps/little-heroes/scripts/pi/screens/run-screens.sh --accept" to keep today's pictures.
# SCREENS_DIR=/home/meshlink/apps/screen-checks

# Kids' tablet internet through Pi-hole (server/netGuardService.js, Parent Portal > Screen Time):
# YouTube Restricted Mode + SafeSearch all day and internet off at bedtime, tablets only. Works with
# no settings: the app uses Pi-hole's CLI password (/etc/pihole/cli_pw, pihole group, see
# scripts/pi/setup-netguard.sh). Undo: node scripts/pi/netguard-undo.mjs
# PIHOLE_URL=http://127.0.0.1
# PIHOLE_PASSWORD=          (an app password, only if the CLI password is turned off)
# NETGUARD_FILE=/home/meshlink/apps/little-heroes-netguard.json
# NETGUARD=off              (turn the feature off)

# Phase 6 one-link consolidation: redirect non-localhost browser visits to the Pi's app port
# straight to the canonical Firebase App Hosting URL (keeps /api/*, /healthz, /phet, and
# 127.0.0.1 Playwright screen checks working locally).
# APP_REDIRECT_URL=https://littleheroes-g1--little-heroes-quest-8842.us-east4.hosted.app

